# ========================================================================
# 22 — OPTIONAL MANUAL CHECKS (not included in Run All)
# ========================================================================
# Gmail positive path: use a disposable account with an email address you
# control; do not use the system ADMIN. Register it or create it via ADMIN,
# save its id, email and original JWT. Use a real mailbox, not .local.
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/forgot-password
# Content-Type: application/json
# {"email":"<mailbox you control>"}
# Expected 202. Copy the fresh token from the email (not the hash in DB).
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/reset-password
# Content-Type: application/json
# {"token":"<fresh token>","newPassword":"CourseFlowChanged2026!"}
# Expected 204. Repeating the same token -> 400. Old JWT/password -> 401.
# Login with new password -> 200.
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/<disposable user id>/password-reset
# Authorization: Bearer {{admin_token}}
# Expected 202. Wait out the 2-minute account cooldown before requesting
# another email; verify the new link, repeat reset with a different password.
#
# Quiz expiration: on a separate temporary module of an active enrolled
# course, create a quiz with timeLimit=1, maxAttempts=1 and one valid question.
# Start attempt -> 201. Wait until expiresAt has passed (at least 60 sec).
# GET /api/quizzes/<quizId>/attempts/<attemptId> -> 200, status=EXPIRED.
# GET /api/quizzes/<quizId>/questions -> 409 after expiry.
# GET /api/users/me/progress and gradebook -> EXPIRED if no completed result.
# POST /api/quizzes/<quizId>/attempts/<attemptId>/submit {"answers":[]}
# -> 409; start another attempt -> 409; history retains expired attempt.
# Do not execute against the main quiz; the main scenario tests attempt limit
# and scoring without real-time sleeps.

# Rate limiting (optional, after main scenario): restart backend or wait 60s.
# Send POST /api/auth/forgot-password 11 times within one minute using
# a non-existent email. First 10 -> 202, request 11 -> 429 with Retry-After.
# Wait the specified number of seconds before repeating.
# Login: max 12 failed attempts per normalized email and 60 per IP
# per one-minute window. The IP limit counts all login attempts.

# Gradebook positive OVERDUE case (optional, no artificial delay in Run All):
# On an active course with an enrolled student, create a new assignment with a
# near-future dueAt. Before dueAt the student matches NOT_SUBMITTED but not OVERDUE
# (provided there are no other overdue missing assignments in the selected module).
# After dueAt, without submitting, GET /api/courses/<courseId>/gradebook?type=ASSIGNMENT&reviewStatus=OVERDUE&moduleId=<moduleId>
# -> 200, student included and the new assignment cell has status OVERDUE.
# NOT_SUBMITTED must still include the student. Delete the unused assignment afterward.

# Deadline reopening (manual): on a separate active course, create an assignment
# with a near-future dueAt, wait for it to expire, then PATCH /api/lessons/<lessonId>/assignments/<assignmentId>/deadline
# with a later future dueAt and current version. Expect 200. An enrolled student
# who has not submitted can now submit -> 201; an existing submission remains unique.
# Verify a teacher of another course receives 403 and an archived course receives 409.

# Grading audit manual verification: find event=submission_graded for scenario 123
# (previousScore=null, newScore=90) and event=submission_regraded for 383 and 387
# (90 -> 95 -> 90). Match assignmentId/submissionId and auditRequestId with HTTP
# X-Request-Id. Rejected scenarios 121, 384 and 385 must not produce a grading event.
# No raw feedback, submission text, email address or credentials in these events.
# Concurrent login: run the existing rate-limit regression after 60 seconds without
# auth traffic. For a separate live stress test, use a unique disposable email and
# 48 parallel valid-shape login requests with an incorrect password from a single
# IP (IP budget 60); complete within one minute: 12 x 401 and 36 x 429. Do not
# run on shared/production accounts. Repeat after an idle window if necessary.
